  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "security-INF-1",
      "file": "internal/server/repos.go",
      "line": 423,
      "checklist": "ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004",
      "effect": "cosmetic",
      "exposure": "eventually",
      "severity": "INFO",
      "fix": "none",
      "claim": "handleRepoMerge, handleRepoSync and handleRepoCherryPick forward r.PathValue(\"branch\")/r.FormValue(\"commit\") straight into internal/repos.Merge/Sync/CherryPick with no format check, while the sibling handleRepoCommits (same file) validates its branch argument through repos.ValidateBranch before use (repos.go:275-283) — an asymmetry this lane cannot resolve because internal/repos/*.go (how Merge/Sync/CherryPick actually invoke worktreeScripts — argv-only exec vs. any shell interpolation) belongs to a different review chunk and was not read here. The bootstrap.go extra-prompt value (BOOTSTRAP_EXTRA_PROMPT) that bootstrapEnv rejects quotes/newlines for also only matters once it reaches cmd/bootstrap/run.sh, likewise outside this chunk.",
      "evidence": "Re-read repos.go in full: handleRepoCommits (line ~259) calls repos.ValidateBranch(r.Context(), branch, repo.Path) before repos.Commits; handleRepoSync (518), handleRepoMerge (423) and handleRepoCherryPick (246) call repos.Sync/Merge/CherryPick directly with the raw path/form value. reposTestEnv's worktree-script stubs (repos_test.go) receive arguments as discrete $*, consistent with argv-style exec rather than shell string interpolation, so no reproducible curl-based exploit could be constructed from this chunk alone; recorded as scope-exclusion per ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004 rather than asserted as a confirmed vulnerability. Station/sibling lane for the repos/cmd chunks should confirm whether Merge/Sync/CherryPick validate or shell-interpolate their argument."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Clean review otherwise: no secrets logged (grepped bootstrap.go/welcome.go/profilesettings.go/routines.go for token/log patterns — token values are never passed to log.Printf or rendered, only paths/labels); the token-verification and style-test bash invocations (welcome.go, profilesettings.go, bootstrap.go) pass all variable data (token path, model, prompt) as quoted positional ($1/$2/$3) argv to `bash -c`, not string-interpolated into the script text, so no shell-injection route; sameOriginGuard (CSRF defense in server.go) is pre-existing and untouched by this diff (confirmed via `git diff` on server.go) so it is not a target of this round; every html/template output in the 13 reviewed .html files relies on Go's default auto-escaping with no template.HTML/template.JS wrapping of request- or config-derived strings in this chunk's files. One scope-exclusion finding (security-INF-1) is recorded above per ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004 for the one asymmetry this lane could see but not resolve without the repos/cmd chunks."
